For the orthorhombic polyethylene unit cell, \(V_{\text{cell}}=(0.741)(0.494)(0.255)=0.09334\ \text{nm}^3\). It contains 4 carbon and 8 hydrogen atoms. Using \(r_C=0.077\ \text{nm}\) and \(r_H=0.046\ \text{nm}\),

\[
\mathrm{APF}=
\frac{4\left(\frac{4\pi}{3}r_C^3\right)+8\left(\frac{4\pi}{3}r_H^3\right)}
{V_{\text{cell}}}
\approx \boxed{0.117}
\]

